 "purpose": "idea of the owner: a remembered pair index k of a key. Arm 1: lazy::at of the commit. Arm 2: skip k pairs with item_skip, compare the key at pair k once, else lazy::at. Arm 3 (deterministic keys): skip to the remembered neighbour k_x, compare keys until one sorts after the key, answer key_not_found. Arm 1 built twice (arm1_AA) for the A/A. Arms over a copy of include/ of the commit with one added friend declaration (hint_probe) in heads, well_formedness, value_sharing and validity.",
 "input": "one map per binary, 8, 32 or 128 pairs, text keys k000, k002, ... in RFC 8949 4.2.1 order, values: pair 1 a nested map {a:1,b:xy}, even pairs small ints, odd pairs short strings. Targets: first, middle (PAIRS/2), last pair; missing key 2*mid+1 between pair mid and mid+1. Per iteration: lazy::from of the next copy (copies fill 2 times the L3) and one lookup",
